{"pagination":{"maxPageableSet":"10000","numFound":2,"query":"name=Goodell&limit=10&title=The Heat Will Kill You First","limit":10,"start":0},"items":{"mods":[{"titleInfo":{"nonSort":{"@space":"preserve","#text":"The  "},"title":"heat will kill you first","subTitle":"life and death on a scorched planet"},"name":[{"@usage":"primary","@type":"personal","namePart":"Goodell, Jeff","role":[{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"creator"}},{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"author."}},{"roleTerm":{"@type":"code","@authority":"marcrelator","#text":"aut"}}]},{"@type":"corporate","namePart":"Little, Brown and Company","role":{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"publisher."}}}],"typeOfResource":"text","genre":[{"@authority":"marcgt","#text":"bibliography"},{"@authority":"rdacontent","#text":"text"},{"@authority":"fast","#text":"Informational works"},{"@authority":"lcgft","#text":"Informational works"},{"@authority":"rvmgf","#text":"Documents d'information."}],"originInfo":[{"place":{"placeTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"nyu"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"New York (State)"}]},"dateIssued":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"2023"},"copyrightDate":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"2023"},"edition":"First edition.","issuance":"monographic"},{"@eventType":"publication","place":{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"New York :"}},"publisher":"Little, Brown and Company,","dateIssued":"2023."}],"language":{"languageTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"English"}]},"physicalDescription":{"form":[{"@authority":"marcform","#text":"print"},{"@type":"media","@authority":"rdamedia","#text":"unmediated"},{"@type":"carrier","@authority":"rdacarrier","#text":"volume"}],"extent":"x, 385 pages ; 25 cm"},"abstract":{"@type":"Summary","#text":"\"The Heat Will Kill You First is about the extreme ways in which our planet is already changing. It is about why spring is coming a few weeks earlier and fall is coming a few weeks later and the impact that will have on everything from our food supply to disease outbreaks. It is about what will happen to our lives and our communities when typical summer days in Chicago or Boston go from 90°F to 110°F. A heatwave, Goodell explains, is a predatory event--one that culls out the most vulnerable people. But that is changing. As heatwaves become more intense and more common, they will become more democratic. As an award-winning journalist who has been at the forefront of environmental journalism for decades, Goodell's new book may be his most provocative yet, explaining how extreme heat will dramatically change the world as we know it\"--"},"tableOfContents":"Prologue: The Goldilocks zone -- A cautionary tale -- How heat shaped us -- Heat islands -- Life on the run -- Anatomy of a crime scene -- Magic valley -- The blob -- The sweat economy -- Ice at the end of the world -- The mosquito is my vector -- Cheap cold air -- What you can't see won't hurt you -- Roast, flee, or act -- The white bear -- Epilogue: Beyond Goldilocks.","targetAudience":{"@authority":"marctarget","#text":"adult"},"note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"Jeff Goodell."},{"@type":"bibliography","#text":"Includes bibliographical references (pages 369-372) and index."}],"subject":[{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Global warming"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Heat waves (Meteorology)"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Climatic changes"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":["Climatic changes","Effect of human beings on"]},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":"Réchauffement de la Terre"},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":"Vagues de chaleur"},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":["Climat","Changements"]},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":["Climat","Changements","Effets de l'homme sur"]},{"@authority":"aat","topic":"global warming"},{"@authority":"aat","topic":"climate change"},{"@authority":"bisacsh","topic":"SCIENCE / Global Warming & Climate Change"},{"@authority":"bisac